OL,3,GNEWSABan foreign nationals from Welsh
OL,4,Ahouse-shares, says Reform
OL,5,
OL,6,FReform has called for foreign nationals
OL,7,Fto be barred from licensed house-shares
OL,8,Fand social housing, in a motion
OL,9,Frejected by a majority of the Senedd.
OL,11,FIn a heated debate on Wednesday, the
OL,12,Fparty argued that houses of multiple
OL,13,Foccupation [HMOs] were the "backbone of
OL,14,Four deranged asylum system" and that
OL,15,F"British citizens must come first".
OL,17,FPlaid Housing Minister Sian Gwenllian
OL,18,Faccused Reform of wanting to turf
OL,19,Ffamilies onto the streets, and said
OL,20,Fonly a small number of HMOs were used
OL,21,Fby asylum seekers.
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
